**Use Lake as a scalpel.** When Lean elaboration is
needed, build the narrowest module with:

```shell
timeout --kill-after=2s 60s lake -q build +Module.Name
```

Every build and check runs through `tool_task`. A
normal check has a 60s external timeout; a known
cold finite computation may be justified up to 300s.
Inspect what rebuilt before raising a bound, and do
not retry an unchanged timeout. For a disposable
probe, use:

```shell
timeout --kill-after=2s 60s lake env lean -j 1 -M 4000 Proofs/Scratch/Probe.lean
```

Keep workspace cache isolation: do not copy build
trees, point `LEAN_PATH` across workspaces, delete
`.lake`, or invent another cache layout. Keep stable
finite computation separate from changing bridges;
explain module cache effects when relevant. Longer
work is allowed when justified and bounded.
